                        "form": "чертёнке"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "414939ed-8413-4d45-84f6-c2533b9120fe",
                        "entry_id": "21eb864b-ecb4-37a7-a09b-7ba6c9ce4022",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "чертеня́тах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "521819e3-7fc8-38d1-85bd-aadc102aa7ec",
                        "entry_id": "21eb864b-ecb4-37a7-a09b-7ba6c9ce4022",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. бойкий, озорной ребенок; шалун"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "42701ec6-1975-4647-9fe1-fb9ec3298555",
                                "sense_id": "521819e3-7fc8-38d1-85bd-aadc102aa7ec",
                                "text": "Вот этот мальчишка действительно рос, как плесень, как вечерняя тень, и, мелькая вороватым чертёнком, всё чаще попадался на глаза."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2550d691-b21e-48c9-b84c-ae7377e5beec",
                                "sense_id": "521819e3-7fc8-38d1-85bd-aadc102aa7ec",
                                "text": "— Ну-ка, слепой чертёнок, ― сказал я, взяв его за ухо, ― говори, куда ты ночью таскался с узлом, а?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c6648c8-8567-3f19-82b0-db00c1242c28",
                        "entry_id": "21eb864b-ecb4-37a7-a09b-7ba6c9ce4022",
                        "glosses": [
                            "уменьш.-ласк. к чёрт"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "103959c6-503c-42d4-b712-6d0f1c489232",
                                "sense_id": "0c6648c8-8567-3f19-82b0-db00c1242c28",
                                "text": "Нагнулся чертёнок в борозду, пошарил, пошарил когтями, выхватил корешок-тройчатку, подал Ивану."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6369f52-aaa1-4014-a27e-985064b7822f",
                                "sense_id": "0c6648c8-8567-3f19-82b0-db00c1242c28",
                                "text": "Голые дети, как чертенята, играли, визжали, гонялись друг за другом возле."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6bce69b-cb35-4643-8e47-989821c4207f",
                                "sense_id": "0c6648c8-8567-3f19-82b0-db00c1242c28",
                                "text": "И какие дерзкие, какие ослепительно гневные глаза выпятила на меня эта белокурая дьяволица, эта маленькая, никогда не доступная моему пониманию помесь ангела с чертёнком!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "317d6f14-fd26-4b48-9b07-7edac6730bea",
                        "source_entry_id": "21eb864b-ecb4-37a7-a09b-7ba6c9ce4022",
                        "target_lang_word": "devil",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "devil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a09acc62-aa1d-3bbd-8896-8f4bf983396c",
                                        "entry_id": "1c702319-8b95-3872-b766-956055ff2ea8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The chief devil; Satan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "devil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b2fd94c-81a8-37ce-ae02-b489c653b46c",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An evil creature, the objectification of a hostile and destructive force."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a1134d47-bcd3-3585-bc08-7e49f404d434",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fictional image of a man, usually red or orange in skin color; with a set of horns on his head, a pointed goatee and a long tail and carrying a pitchfork; that represents evil and portrayed to children in an effort to discourage bad behavior."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39683b03-37b8-3c35-b8ee-dbf01fbe1653",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The bad part of the conscience; the opposite to the angel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e8440a4-070b-4831-8210-cdc903ee7113",
                                                "sense_id": "39683b03-37b8-3c35-b8ee-dbf01fbe1653",
                                                "text": "The devil in me wants to let him suffer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7f933d9-ccde-3178-b37f-e489c7909eab",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wicked or naughty person, or one who harbors reckless, spirited energy, especially in a mischievous way; usually said of a young child."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ef5666c-30d9-4112-a23b-ebdb441f8156",
                                                "sense_id": "d7f933d9-ccde-3178-b37f-e489c7909eab",
                                                "text": "Those two kids are devils in a toy store."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b086e32c-3894-33b9-b4b9-41bbf1b20332",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thing that is awkward or difficult to understand or do."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ed2f2db-6e00-4995-b1a6-98e208523d78",
                                                "sense_id": "b086e32c-3894-33b9-b4b9-41bbf1b20332",
                                                "text": "That math problem was a devil."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d153552c-bc61-394d-aabe-d302ef071937",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hell."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "euphemistic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90e98319-bb46-4075-bb93-eb4a7386780d",
                                                "sense_id": "d153552c-bc61-394d-aabe-d302ef071937",
                                                "text": "What in the devil is that?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29c27562-eac4-44ba-a3c6-bbabcfa2debb",
                                                "sense_id": "d153552c-bc61-394d-aabe-d302ef071937",
                                                "text": "What the devil is that?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eff9ffd4-f001-472c-bd83-4be962403392",
                                                "sense_id": "d153552c-bc61-394d-aabe-d302ef071937",
                                                "text": "She is having a devil of a time fixing it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ae108f0-e3ed-4f1b-93f6-cea8c80a4b48",
                                                "sense_id": "d153552c-bc61-394d-aabe-d302ef071937",
                                                "text": "You can go to the devil for all I care."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "239d40c6-e6fc-3d85-8f33-07f741990ea3",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person, especially a man; used to express a particular opinion of him, usually in the phrases poor devil and lucky devil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e644f82-7f32-3510-8e83-f1d1fcb130b1",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A printer's assistant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58746e3a-b615-44ef-8c27-98dd219e7f52",
                                                "sense_id": "6e644f82-7f32-3510-8e83-f1d1fcb130b1",
                                                "text": "For he will not leave his listener to dwell upon sorrow when the print office beckons and he can show you what a good little devil he became."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3fee90ea-f41a-3115-8d13-0ec76254753d",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A poltergeist that haunts printing works."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "India"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "238aff64-5c63-3489-9daf-fccf1351c296",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dust devil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02e0a41f-68ac-4c27-a870-c8692dbba63f",
                                                "sense_id": "238aff64-5c63-3489-9daf-fccf1351c296",
                                                "text": "The formation of tornados and water-spouts is very probably identical with that of dust-storms and \"devils,\" viz., a sudden disturbance of the vertical equilibrium of the atmosphere, where by an upward rush of air is generated, which rapidly becomes spiral."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c15dc6c5-d239-4e3c-a544-bf11716d7154",
                                                "sense_id": "238aff64-5c63-3489-9daf-fccf1351c296",
                                                "text": "There are few sights more appalling than a sandstorm in the desert, the \"Zauba'ah\" as the Arabs call it. Devils, or pillars of sand, vertical and inclined, measuring a thousand feet high[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71f0d068-9cbf-3c74-b34d-00699f2e6c97",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A barren, unproductive and unused area."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "in-compounds"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "957dcc26-62e3-4c12-a3f7-48f97c632ad7",
                                                "sense_id": "71f0d068-9cbf-3c74-b34d-00699f2e6c97",
                                                "text": "devil strip"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be32a1ed-5e1d-3f4a-9890-e80413a58e73",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dish, as a bone with the meat, broiled and excessively peppered; a grill with Cayenne pepper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a129c7e-6c83-488b-abc2-225855c71eb6",
                                                "sense_id": "be32a1ed-5e1d-3f4a-9890-e80413a58e73",
                                                "text": "Men and women busy in baking, broiling, roasting oysters, and preparing devils on the gridiron."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61bb9104-65d6-3b06-b390-988bd033b062",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A machine for tearing or cutting rags, cotton, etc., as used in the production of mungo or shoddy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "313fcf76-c6cc-4aad-8e8c-583cf9ca5758",
                                                "sense_id": "61bb9104-65d6-3b06-b390-988bd033b062",
                                                "text": "The woollen things are torn to pieces by a machine having spiked rollers (termed a devil), cleansed, and the fibre spun with a certain proportion of new wool, the yarn being afterwards woven into the full-bodied but flimsy fabric termed shoddy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6f58928-8075-3855-b925-52f2ef5d7f37",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Tasmanian devil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6388cb0b-4038-42b4-a809-712192595817",
                                                "sense_id": "c6f58928-8075-3855-b925-52f2ef5d7f37",
                                                "text": "He removes his food, water, and torch from the pack and then pushes it to the far end of the tent – no devil is going to rip his pack apart tonight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43cd1868-69e8-4964-83a1-426842a1439b",
                                                "sense_id": "c6f58928-8075-3855-b925-52f2ef5d7f37",
                                                "text": "In the 1800s, for example, workers at a wool company were scared that the devils would attack their sheep."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e0cfcc4-8f4e-3ace-82c6-29a8aafde1f0",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An endurance event where riders who fall behind are periodically eliminated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7501891-a791-35b3-b33c-389e6ca4aa07",
                                        "entry_id": "6da9dd30-bf5b-3e6c-9758-57a6efad6344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of devil seam (“the seam between garboard strake and the keel, on wooden boats”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "devil",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89ce15d9-b795-30a9-b194-550d3c4a37c3",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make like a devil; to invest with the character of a devil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "289e12f3-4b4a-34c5-a37d-bcc08fed8fe8",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To annoy or bother."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d133a1b0-480a-3e06-ac15-79125adf6c89",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work as a ‘devil’; to work for a lawyer or writer without fee or recognition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f21317ed-c571-4cf1-8e6f-d6a87411c9d0",
                                                "sense_id": "d133a1b0-480a-3e06-ac15-79125adf6c89",
                                                "text": "He did not repeat the scathing estimate of her character by Quatrefages, who at that time spent one afternoon a week devilling at the Consulate, keeping the petty-cash box in order."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a8f7b33-07ad-3094-889a-acfb0f3d493c",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To ghostwrite; to author while working as a ‘devil’."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d08a8ac-c708-4ddd-a6a2-d34bf44ba7cb",
                                                "sense_id": "0a8f7b33-07ad-3094-889a-acfb0f3d493c",
                                                "text": "Didn't secretaries write the speeches of Parliamentary \"big-bugs\"? Weren't the opinions of eminent lawyers often written by their juniors, read over and signed? Weren't briefs and pleadings devilled?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6c704bf-42f4-3822-adfe-7897d0e18c4f",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare (food) with spices, making it spicy:",
                                            "To grill with cayenne pepper; to season highly in cooking, as with pepper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e34834e2-8240-45c9-b9f0-57e5b0dac3db",
                                                "sense_id": "a6c704bf-42f4-3822-adfe-7897d0e18c4f",
                                                "text": "[…]; you could watch a buckwheat pancake whirled into existence under your eyes and see fowls' legs devilled, peppered, grilled, and tormented till they lost all semblance of the original Mariposa chicken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7782430d-f02a-3441-ba9c-16b41f079ad4",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare (food) with spices, making it spicy:",
                                            "To finely grind cooked ham or other meat with spices and condiments."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "305c17b5-d127-39aa-a8eb-b6b9d502a3cb",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prepare (food) with spices, making it spicy:",
                                            "To prepare a sidedish of shelled halved boiled eggs to whose extracted yolks are added condiments and spices, which mixture then is placed into the halved whites to be served."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb2fe23f-f639-4dd3-84d3-d4247fdf340d",
                                                "sense_id": "305c17b5-d127-39aa-a8eb-b6b9d502a3cb",
                                                "text": "She's going to devil four dozen eggs for the picnic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "caa2e146-1b4f-319a-b498-1e5a772c9f33",
                                        "entry_id": "95273d59-a143-37b4-acf9-31d29563a06f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shred fabric into its fibres for recycling, as in the production of mungo or shoddy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fde7c6e0-d79d-465e-b3f0-1783915b7af9",
                                                "sense_id": "caa2e146-1b4f-319a-b498-1e5a772c9f33",
                                                "text": "Tailors' clippings and remnants of fine woollen goods, such as broadcloth, etc., are devilled and spun into yarn for making cloth of nicer quality, called mungo."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
